{
  "requirement": "The `requirement` string in each evidence file MUST match all Markdown inside its fenced `{req}` directive, excluding leading and trailing whitespace. Habeas MUST report changed requirement text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment:** the requirement is implemented and tested. I found no unmarked implementation and no unspecified behavior under its marker.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `validate_evidence_file` (`src/evidence.rs`, marked `{impl}` at the `// {impl}`requirements.ci.requirement_text`` comment) reads the evidence string from the `requirement` field. For an example it uses the `example` field, through `kind.noun()`.\n- It compares that string for exact equality with the declaration's current `expected.text`. Unequal text produces a validation error, `\"<label>: requirement text changed (<source>)\"`, followed by `compact_diff` output (`- old` / `+ new` lines). This is the \"MUST report changed requirement text\" obligation.\n- The expected text comes from `collect_definitions`. That function takes `without_options(content, block.body_start..block.body_end, ..)` and trims it. The span is everything between the fences, including headings, code blocks and nested fences.\n- The text-extraction side is carried by `requirements.ci.span`, which states: \"Leading and trailing whitespace MUST be excluded when comparing the body with evidence.\" The `// {impl}`requirements.ci.span`` marker in `collect_definitions` covers it, so it is not an unmarked gap.\n- `without_options` (`src/lib.rs`) is marked `{impl}` for this requirement. It removes `:impl:` and `:test:` option lines from the compared text, as `requirements.references.anchors` specifies.\n- The \"must not be empty\" check on the text field sits under the requirement_text marker. It is a minor schema-style check and does not contradict the requirement.\n\n**Tests**\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` is the positive case. It uses a multi-line body containing a code fence with a literal `{req}`, and the evidence string matches the body, so no errors result.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` is the failure case. A stale \"Old text.\" produces \"requirement text changed\" with the `- Old text.` / `+ First.` diff. A non-string `requirement` is also reported (\"requirement must be a string\").\n- `anchored_files_must_be_completely_covered_and_resolvable` checks that `:impl:` / `:test:` option lines are excluded from the compared text, for both a requirement and an example. It asserts there is no \"text changed\" error.\n- `requirement_bodies_are_compared_without_surrounding_whitespace` (marked `ci.span`) and `compact_diffs_elide_common_lines_and_truncate_long_runs` cover whitespace trimming and the diff format. Together these cover the match, changed-text and option-exclusion cases.\n\n**Minor gap, not blocking:** no test records evidence text with stray surrounding whitespace. The exact-equality comparison against the trimmed text is a reasonable reading of \"excluding leading and trailing whitespace\".",
